        "original_id": "4e6a5abb-fd97-5731-9318-22d15b81953e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Gambon, Albus Dumbledore, Richard Harris, Anna Shaffer\n- Organizations: BBC, ITV, Order of the Phoenix\n- Products: The Singing Detective, Maigret, Harry Potter films, Hollyoaks, Otherwise Engaged\n- Roles: Jules Maigret, Professor Albus Dumbledore, Romilda Vane, Ruby Button\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Michael Gambon took over from Bates in Otherwise Engaged and played the role for a year, eight times a week.\n- In the 1990s, Michael Gambon played Jules Maigret in ITV's serial Maigret.\n- Michael Gambon played the title mystery-writer protagonist in the BBC television serial The Singing Detective.\n- After Richard Harris died, Michael Gambon played Professor Albus Dumbledore in the final six Harry Potter films.\n- Albus Dumbledore is the founder and leader of the Order of the Phoenix, an organisation dedicated to fighting Lord Voldemort.\n- Anna Shaffer was born on 15 March 1992.\n- Anna Shaffer is an English actress best known for playing Ruby Button in Hollyoaks and Romilda Vane in the Harry Potter film series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
